      "math_academy_id": "e-13065",
      "problem": "If ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146952/assets/3555f7befd80c535eda4bd5e8e3988c13e7caae3ab98341e543630948b4b789c.svg) then ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146952/assets/433617fee04ae1c29fefa6eb3b3556dae765f35b7978d35bd463b9444d145bce.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Using the relationship between multiplication and division, we can write our problem as follows:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14146952/assets/fee4b12010c92a06b0d5a8e9887110b562cfc308466560ab6729ffc2b9b3043f.svg)\n\nWe can simplify this fraction as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{7}{35} = \\dfrac{7 \\div 7}{35 \\div 7} = \\dfrac{1}{5}\n$$\n\nTo write this fraction as a percentage, we write an equivalent fraction with $100$ as the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{5} = \\dfrac{1 \\times 20}{5 \\times 20} = \\dfrac{20}{100}\n$$\n\nNow we can write this fraction as a percentage:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{20}{100} = 20\\%\n$$",
